WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.589
If you have a real problem, Brainstorming
is a good way to come up with a solution

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:10.170
or two. As the name suggests, the idea is
that you storm on the neural pathways

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:14.969
through the brain to pick a lot of
thoughts quickly and intuitively. It's

00:00:14.969 --> 00:00:19.109
best to do this with a group of diverse
people, so you have lots of different

00:00:19.109 --> 00:00:24.539
brains to explore. This leads to the
creation of more ideas and maybe new

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:30.740
solutions. Before you start make sure you
solve the right problem.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:36.270
Einstein said, to solve a problem "I would
spend 55 minutes defining the problem

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:41.550
and then five minutes solving it." Tina
Seelig, a well-known professor on

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:47.399
creativity, teaches to define a problem
by reframing the question for example by

00:00:47.399 --> 00:00:53.250
simply asking "why?" Say you brainstorm
ideas for a birthday party for your mum,

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:58.829
you can ask: "Why do we organize birthday parties?" You might then realize that we

00:00:58.829 --> 00:01:04.729
do them to make people feel special then
ask "how can I make my mum feel special?"

00:01:04.729 --> 00:01:12.119
Now a totally different idea might come
up. Once you define the real problem,

00:01:12.119 --> 00:01:19.680
start! Here are three ways. Guided Group
Brainstorming: First get some markers and

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:24.930
a whiteboard or some post-it notes. Then
invite the participants, these are your

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:30.509
brains. Company bosses, teachers or other authorities are advised to stay outside

00:01:30.509 --> 00:01:37.159
or facilitate, their authority can
intimidate shy people from speaking up.

00:01:37.159 --> 00:01:43.829
Then lay out the four ground rules of
brainstorming. 1: Go for quantity - get

00:01:43.829 --> 00:01:50.399
out all the ideas no matter how silly. 2:
Withhold criticism. There are no bad

00:01:50.399 --> 00:01:59.070
ideas. 3: Welcome crazy ideas - the wilder
the better. 4: Build on other people's

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:04.759
ideas - listen to them first and then add
"yes and..."

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:10.900
Now you can start. Write the problem as a
question on the whiteboard. Then ask all

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:16.000
of your brains to throw in their ideas.
As a facilitator, keep the discussion

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.560
focused on the topic. To ensure that
people don't speak over one another, you

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:25.300
can provide a talking stick which is
passed around. Note down all the ideas

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:31.060
and put them up for everyone to see.
Remind people to add on to ideas. If Anne

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:37.450
thinks of: "Let's build a cool umbrella"
Jay can say "YES AND let's make it one that

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:42.940
flies too..." If someone did kill a good
idea, the facilitator can always bring it

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:46.620
back to life to throw it back on the
table.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.790
At the end of the session, see if there
are two ideas that can be combined. In

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:58.330
brainstorming, the slogan is: 1+1=3 then let the team vote to

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:02.650
know which of the most popular ones. You can now either start with another round

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:07.060
of brainstorming to build on those ideas,
or if you are happy with the solution,

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:15.070
bring it to an end. Finally record your
best ideas, so you don't lose them.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:19.540
The Nominal Group Technique: Explain the ground rules and present the problem.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:25.480
Then ask each person to write their
ideas anonymously. Then collect the ideas

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:31.120
and let the group vote on each idea. The
top-ranked ideas may be sent back to the

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:36.370
participants or sub groups for further
brainstorming. For example, one group may

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:40.630
brainstorm on the form of a product,
while the other focuses on the technical

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:48.850
features. The Group Passing Technique: Let people sit in a circle, explain the rules

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:54.489
and present the problem each person
writes down one idea and then passes the

00:03:54.489 --> 00:03:59.320
piece of paper to the next person who
adds some thoughts. This continues until

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:05.110
everybody gets his or her original piece
of paper back. By this time, it is likely

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:09.940
that the group will have extensively
elaborated on each idea. Let everyone

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:16.190
explain their evolved idea and write
each one up. You can then let the group vote.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:22.350
If you want to brainstorm by yourself,
give it a try right now. At the end of

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:27.390
this scene we will present you with a
problem once you get it right five ideas

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:32.370
in the comments below as fast as you can without much thinking. This unlocks your

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:36.750
creativity and gets you past mental
blocks. After you are done,

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:41.070
read the comments from the others. Pick
your favourite idea and build your

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:46.110
thought on top of it. To do that, just
reply to that person starting with "yes

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:54.419
and..." Here's the problem: Our oceans are
full of plastic waste. A lot of it is

00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:59.490
eaten by fish with uncertain effects on
our health. According to The Economist

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:05.010
Newspaper, by 2050 the oceans could
contain more plastic than fish, measured

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:11.990
in weight. So: "How can we reduce the
plastic waste in our oceans today?"

